memoryAccess is capability
memoryAccess purpose "Authority to read and write threads' records, mutexes, and condition variables"
memoryAccess grants use machine.memory none

systemCalls is capability
systemCalls purpose "Authority to start threads, wait on futexes, sleep, and yield"
systemCalls grants use system.calls none

# D-166: a thread (thrd_t, the address of its record: a heap block of 64 bytes: 0 its thread id, which the kernel
# clears and wakes when the thread ends (CLONE_CHILD_CLEARTID), 8 what it gave, 16 its stack, 24 the stack's size, 32
# its thread block, 40 whether it is detached, 48 the function, 56 its argument) runs on a stack of 8 MiB and a thread
# block of its own (the thread pointer: on x86_64 the stack protector's canary at 0x28, copied from the first
# thread's, and errno at 0x40). A mutex (mtx_t, glibc's 40 bytes) is 0 its state (0 free, 1 held, 2 held with
# waiters), 8 its owner's thread id, 16 how many times a recursive one is held, 24 its kind; a condition variable
# (cnd_t, 48 bytes) is 0 a sequence the waiters wait on. Thread-specific storage keeps 64 keys, each thread's values in
# its block from 0x80. On Windows (D-168) a thread is CreateThread's, its block in a thread-local slot, and a wait
# sleeps a millisecond and looks again.
# machine.state bytes 28480 to 28999 and 29000 to 29007 (the thread-local slot's index plus 1) belong to this module: 28480 the first thread's record, 28488 how many keys
# were made, 28496 the block of each key's destructor (64 keys), 28504 the block of the first thread's values.
success is constant
success purpose "thrd_success: the call did what it was asked"
success type Int32
success value 0

busy is constant
busy purpose "thrd_busy: another thread holds the mutex"
busy type Int32
busy value 1

error is constant
error purpose "thrd_error: the call could not do what it was asked"
error type Int32
error value 2

timedOut is constant
timedOut purpose "thrd_timedout: the deadline passed first"
timedOut type Int32
timedOut value 4

stackBytes is constant
stackBytes purpose "A thread's stack: 8 MiB"
stackBytes type Int64
stackBytes value 8388608

forever is constant
forever purpose "The bound of a loop that ends when its work does"
forever type Int64
forever value 9223372036854775807

firstRecordAt is constant
firstRecordAt purpose "Where the first thread's record is kept, in machine.state (0 until thrd_current asks)"
firstRecordAt type Int64
firstRecordAt value 28480

keysAt is constant
keysAt purpose "Where how many thread-specific keys were made is kept, in machine.state"
keysAt type Int64
keysAt value 28488

destructorsAt is constant
destructorsAt purpose "Where the block of each key's destructor is kept, in machine.state"
destructorsAt type Int64
destructorsAt value 28496

firstValuesAt is constant
firstValuesAt purpose "Where the block of the first thread's thread-specific values is kept, in machine.state"
firstValuesAt type Int64
firstValuesAt value 28504

